{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793307424,"nonce":"IERACEXaeGTiy3AgUbwNc09RQ3o=","message":"The planner now admits supported inline overlay roots as local native groups while returning an ownership boundary to ordinary ancestors. GPU shared-layer capture keeps groups inside overlay scopes in their dynamic owner instead of retaining the static paint anchor. Opaque roots retain a boundary too, so images do not return to the early static-image route at opacity one. No public API, shader, primitive/instance, FFI or stable-ID changes.\n\nEight new controls pass normally: /private/tmp/blinc-overlay-group-all.log. They cover snapshot/direct/compositor frames, plain/styled text, SVGs, images, foreground canvases, root foreground/background ownership, effects/endpoints, text modes, 1x/4x and DPI1/2; binding/CSS motion and path clips; sibling ordering and root replacement; callbacks/meshes; entry-motion/snapshot interleaving; and capability/ancestor/material/nested-root fallback guards. The capability effect control now checks dynamic capture for a supported portal instead of classifying it solely with unsupported owners.\n\nThe first live-motion fixture put a motion wrapper outside the overlay root. It failed at mode1/source0/opacity.5 in /private/tmp/blinc-overlay-group-live.log. That is still an unsupported ordinary moving ancestor and is not certified by this child. Existing OverlayStack/ToastTray place animation inside the overlay root; the passing binding fixture follows that structure. The outside-wrapper case remains explicitly guarded by metadata fallback and must remain in parent e0a7502. Initial Image builder/lifetime and tone-mapped mesh presence fixture errors were corrected without production accommodations.\n\nScope excludes dedicated render_overlay_tree_with_motion, unsupported nested portals and glass/flow/3D descendants or ancestors, and ordinary ancestor groups spanning the portal boundary. Metadata fallback is not pixel-correctness certification for those combinations. No broad release-ready claim.\n\nRoot capture adds paired command metadata and conservative repaint for shared dynamic content. Opacity/effect groups use the existing bounded texture pool and bake path; opaque identity groups flatten when eligible. GPU callbacks/meshes retain their existing temporary frame textures. Vertex/image payload policy is unchanged. No frame-time or peak-memory measurement is claimed. Scoped lint/adjacent controls and DT/restored probes are running, jobs=2/capacities=1024, offscreen only. No push or publication.","files":null}]}